      {
        "text": "John Harabedian represents the 41st District in the California State Assembly, elected in 2024. He was previously a Sierra Madre city council member and mayor, an attorney and prosecutor, and a Clean Power Alliance founding board member. His campaign says he supports expanding mental health services and affordable housing, strengthening gun safety laws, and defending abortion rights. In 2025, he authored the MENA Inclusion Act to expand demographic data collection for Middle Eastern and North African communities. He authored bills on mortgage forbearance and contamination testing for wildfire survivors, and initiated a state audit of the Eaton and Palisades fires emergency response. He proposed a state-led housing recovery task force. He chairs the Joint Legislative Audit Committee.",
